WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.930
Marvel's newest round of Infinity War toys
have once again revealed perhaps a bit too

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.350
much about an upcoming movie in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.099
In case you don't remember, Thor: Ragnarok
saw the Odinson lose his right eye in a battle

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:16.200
with his villainous sister Hela, the Goddess
of Death.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.730
While losing an eye barely inconvenienced
the God of Thunder in combat, it did mangle

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.170
his look, leaving the hero bruised and battered
and shorn of his locks by the end of Ragnarok,

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.260
where Infinity War picks up.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.780
"Who the hell are you guys?"

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.540
Hasbro's assortment of Infinity War toys,
as well as Funko's bobbleheads, have made

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:41.090
it perfectly clear that Thor doesn't lose
his eye permanently.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.690
In fact, he seems to get it back in time for
whatever big battle the Avengers have against

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.690
Thanos.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.719
But a few toys tell a slightly larger story.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:54.310
Hasbro's Marvel Legends three-pack gives us
a Thor with an eyepatch, hanging out with

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:59.760
Rocket and a teen-aged Groot - a trio that's
repeated in a LEGO set and Hot Toys' teaser

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.610
photos for their own Infinity War action figures.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.390
A later wave of Marvel Legends includes a
second Thor, this time with two working eyes

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.990
and a fancy new axe… with a handle made
of Groot.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:15.909
New Cosbaby figures from Hot Toys also appear
to show the full evolution in Thor's status

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.540
quo, fixing a setback the character suffered
in his most recent solo movie.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.940
If they do indeed reflect the events of Infinity
War, the two Thor figures seem to tell a little

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.530
story of personal growth and triumph for the
mythical Asgardian fighter.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.170
The first figure shows Thor with an eyepatch,
charging himself up for combat, Dragon Ball

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.350
Z style.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:40.700
He still sports the scars of his battle with
Hela, with only one lightning-charged eye

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.700
visible.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.939
All is as expected.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:47.970
The second figure introduces a two-eyed Thor
with new armor and a new weapon.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:52.040
Scarring around the figure's right eye is
consistent with the damage Hela caused, with

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:57.480
one big difference: The eyeball is back, suggesting
that the God of Thunder is going to regenerate

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.299
his eye as a part of the push against Thanos.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:05.860
While audiences have seen Thor spontaneously
generate magical armor around his body before,

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.220
we've never seen him regrow an actual body
part.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.780
If all this turns out to be true, it begs
the question — why hasn't he re-grown his

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.780
hair?

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.290
"Life is about growth, it's about change."

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.310
Previously, a toy called the Hulk-Out Hulkbuster
seemed to confirm a major moment from the

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.370
upcoming superhero movie, revealing that Bruce
Banner will wear one of Tony Stark's Hulkbuster

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.450
Iron Man suits before going green inside of
it, bursting out of the armor like a vengeful,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.090
angry nesting doll.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.090
"Wow."

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:39.120
However, it's worth noting that these tie-in
products aren't always on the money, with

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.810
occasional liberties being taken with the
story for the sake of making a kickass toy.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:48.760
Previous reports that a Lego set had revealed
Thor to be using the comic book weapon Jarnbjorn

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.569
in Infinity War turned out to be not quite
accurate; it was later confirmed that Thor's

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:57.480
weapon in the movie would be an axe called
Stormbreaker.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.100
So as fun as it is, and as accurate as it
might end up being, it's still worth taking

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.100
all of this toy-sourced information with a
healthy abundance of salt.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.420
We'll be able to see for ourselves what happens
to Thor in Avengers: Infinity War when the

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.659
movie launches in theaters worldwide on April
27th.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:14.659
"Ready?"

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:15.659
Thanks for watching!

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:18.269
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:20.260
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

